R-CH13 R-CH16 R-NS4 R-SC10 R-SC13 (slice 240, Design Q612): an installed user build is usable by its id when its channel has NO table in config.toml (the channel was removed, R-CH13). The build was installed with `channel` and `source` in .talon.json. `tln roc default <id>` writes the default with no network and no channel table; a unique prefix of the id gives the full id (R-SC10); the full id again: already the default (the default is a user id now, R-CH5: `default-roc` holds a user-channel id; today the config check refuses it: red); --json has the envelope of roc/df1-default. The calls.log of run 1 is that of the current code (it is green with the full id; the prefix run is expected to need the same calls); the lines of runs 2 and 3 are a proposal. The probe result under the id is tested in 241 (Design Q615 item 3).
